{"segs": ["PA_ja_123:0.2", "PA_ja_123:0.3"], "en": "The First Book, The Chapter on the Kusa Reed (Kusanāḷivagga)", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:48:33Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_123:0.4"], "en": "3. The Naṅgalīsajātaka:", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:48:33Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_123:1.1", "PA_ja_123:1.2"], "en": "“The fool speaks words that lead everywhere, in every situation.”", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:48:33Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_123:1.3"], "en": "\"This one does not know curd nor the plowman;", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:48:33Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_123:1.4"], "en": "he mistakes the curd for the plowman.", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:48:33Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_123:2.1"], "en": "Thus ends the third Jātaka, the Naṅgalīsajātaka.", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:48:33Z"}
